[00:15.11]Hello darkness, my old friend,
[00:23.14]I've come to talk with you again,
[00:31.42]Because a vision softly creeping,
[00:39.11]Left its seeds while I was sleeping,
[00:47.38]And the vision that was planted in my brain,
[00:57.42]Still remains,
[01:03.11]Within the sound of silence.
[01:12.76]In restless dreams I walked alone,
[01:20.35]Narrow streets of cobblestone,
[01:28.14]Beneath the halo of a street lamp,
[01:36.00]I turned my collar to the cold and damp,
[01:43.99]When my eyes were stabbed by the flash of a neon light,
[01:54.08]That split the night,
[01:59.78]And touched the sound of silence.
[02:08.85]And in the naked light I saw,
[02:16.59]Ten thousand people, maybe more,
[02:24.78]People talking without speaking,
[02:32.84]People hearing without listening,
[02:40.80]People writing songs that voices never share,
[02:50.48]And no one dare,
[02:56.29]Disturb the sound of silence.
[03:04.29]"Fools" said I, "You do not know,
[03:13.06]Silence like a cancer grows,
[03:20.73]Hear my words that I might teach you,
[03:28.85]Take my arms that I might reach you,"
[03:36.56]But my words, like silent raindrops fell,
[03:46.49]And echoed in the wells of silence.
[03:58.74]And the people bowed and prayed,
[04:08.31]To the neon god they made,
[04:16.03]And the sign flashed out its warning,
[04:23.71]In the words that it was forming,
[04:31.55]And the sign said "The words of the prophets are written on the subway walls,
[04:42.89]And tenement halls,
[04:48.33]And whispered in the sounds,
[04:58.85]Of silence."